OL,3,GNEWSAThe 1600s pioneer who challenged
OL,4,Aearth's origins
OL,5,
OL,6,FRyland-Epton said it was "staggering"
OL,7,Fhow much was left out of the Victorian
OL,8,Fedition. Her transcription is more than
OL,9,F400 pages - the 1800s version stands at
OL,10,Fabout 100 pages.
OL,12,FAubrey, who was also an early
OL,13,Farchaeologist, mathematician and
OL,14,Ffounding member of the Royal Society,
OL,15,Fquestioned the age of the earth in the
OL,16,Fbook and wrote about environmental
OL,17,Fissues, lamenting deforestation and the
OL,18,Fimpact it had on wildlife.
